        ["e-", "out", "Latin e, ex, out of", [["elimination reaction", "a putting out (Latin eliminare, from e- + limen, threshold): a hydrogen and the leaving group leave from neighbouring carbons and a pi bond forms between them, the E of E1 and E2"]]],
        ["uni-", "one", "Latin unus, one", [["unimolecular", "one species in the slow step: rate = k[substrate], the 1 of SN1 and E1"]], { "auto": false }],
        ["bi-", "two", "Latin bi-, bis, twice", [["bimolecular", "two species in the slow step: rate = k[substrate][nucleophile or base], the 2 of SN2 and E2"]]],
        ["intra-", "within", "Latin intra, within", [["intramolecular", "within one molecule: the nucleophile and the leaving group sit in the same molecule, so SN2 closes a ring"], ["intramolecular SN2", "an SN2 inside one molecule: the same two arrows and the same backside attack, and the product is a ring"]], { "auto": false }]
